> You're confusing it with Demonbane.  Excalibur has drain resistance, 
> searching, +d5 Hit, +d10 Damage, and that's it.  At least in Nethack, 
> I don't know about Slash'em.  

The same, although in SLASH'EM drain resistance is far more important 
than in vanilla ("The gnome zaps a curved wand! Goodbye level 5."). 
Excalibur in SLASH'EM also improves the chances of successful automatic 
searching, which is handy. (I don't -think- it has this feature in 
vanilla.)

(Note that you can #twoweapon artifacts in SLASH'EM, although the off-
handed one loses some properties, particularly special attacks. Excalibur's
search and drain resistance properties work just fine in the off-hand.)

That said, I rather like Excalibur, although in vanilla it's useful
mainly because it's especially easy for lawfuls to get early in the 
game; in the later stages, it's usually worth using a higher damage
weapon unless you need the intrinsics. 

Mjollnir's a double-edged hammer, to butcher a phrase. I think fondly
of it; my first ascension was a valk with the hammer (In the tourney a
couple years ago). It -does- put out a lot of damage, but it also has
a bad habit of destroying wands and jewelry. Until you have everything
you want in those departments (and backups!), I'd stick to Grayswandir,
Excalibur, Snickersnee, or something else less volatile.

